{
 "schema": "operand_replay_phase_residency_reference_v1",
 "mechanism": "operand_replay_phase_residency",
 "hardware_id": "metax_c500",
 "allowed_use": "Evidence that a second read of the same operand tile costs no DRAM traffic when it is adjacent to the first, and exactly doubles it once the swept footprint exceeds L2 when the two are a full sweep apart.  Bounds how much DRAM traffic an L2-ingress stream multiplicity of two can account for.",
 "forbidden_use": "Any duration.  Not an L2 capacity value, a DRAM bandwidth, a replacement policy, or a per-shape traffic correction.  It does not state which phase any production kernel uses.",
 "production_or_evaluation_duration_consumed": false,
 "instrument": "mcProfiler perf_exec --custom --per-kernel, one marker window, one numbered per-invocation file per ordinal",
 "counters": [
  "Global Memory Read bytes",
  "Global Memory Write bytes",
  "L2C Hit Rate"
 ],
 "geometry": {
  "block_threads": 256,
  "tile_bytes": 4096,
  "workers": 104,
  "addressing": "disjoint contiguous per-worker partitions",
  "note": "grid, block, footprint and total logical read bytes are identical between the two phases of each pair"
 },
 "why_independent_axes": "The canonical MetaX BM64 fused-MoE launch records operand_replay_a = operand_replay_b = 2, an L2-ingress counter identity whose own docstring states it is not a cross-tile replay law: it does not say where in the k loop the second crossing falls.  The two possibilities have opposite DRAM consequences, so the phase must be measured before the multiplicity can be given any DRAM meaning.  This probe carries no routing, no expert blocking, no MMA and no epilogue -- only the double read whose phase is in question.",
 "finding": "The phase is load-bearing and its transition sits at the L2 size.  Adjacent double reads cost 1.02x the footprint at every footprint tested, from 2 to 128 MiB: the second read is always served by the line the first allocated.  Separated double reads cost 1.02x at 2 MiB, 1.46x at 8 MiB and saturate at 2.03x from 32 MiB upward.  Repeatability is exact at 32 MiB (32.5 against 32.5 MiB adjacent, 65.0 against 65.0 MiB separated).  An L2-ingress multiplicity of two can therefore account for at most a factor of two of DRAM traffic, and only above L2.",
 "build": {
  "compiler": "/opt/maca/mxgpu_llvm/bin/mxcc",
  "flags": "-x maca -offload-arch native --maca-path=/opt/maca -O3",
  "source": "microbench/metax_c500/memory/l2/operand_replay_phase_residency.cpp",
  "binary_sha256": "a0f2e6ca249a2068c93b1d69996bb1b42cd98c1e474ae4f1337c69a84245a0ff"
 },
